# PowerShell File System Operations Guide  

---

## 1. Listing Files & Folders  
**Core Cmdlet**: `Get-ChildItem`  

### Command Syntax  
```powershell  
# Basic listing  
Get-ChildItem -Path C:\ -Force  

# Recursive scan  
Get-ChildItem -Path C:\ -Force -Recurse  
```  

### Filtering Rules  
```powershell  
# Advanced filtering example  
Get-ChildItem -Path $env:ProgramFiles -Recurse -Include *.exe |  
    Where-Object {  
        ($_.LastWriteTime -gt '2005-10-01') -and  
        ($_.Length -ge 1MB) -and  
        ($_.Length -le 10MB)  
    }  
```  

**Key Parameters**:  
• `-Path`: Target directory  
• `-Force`: Show hidden/system items  
• `-Recurse`: Include subdirectories  
• `-Include`: File pattern filter  

---

## 2. Copy Operations  
**Core Cmdlet**: `Copy-Item`  

### File Backup  
```powershell  
if (Test-Path -Path $PROFILE) {  
    Copy-Item -Path $PROFILE -Destination ($PROFILE -replace 'ps1$', 'bak') -Force  
}  
```  

### Folder Replication  
```powershell  
Copy-Item -Path C:\temp\test1 -Destination C:\temp\DeleteMe -Recurse -Confirm:$false  
```  

**Safety Protocol**:  
• Always test with `-WhatIf` first:  
```powershell  
Copy-Item -Filter *.txt -Path c:\data -Recurse -Destination C:\temp\text -WhatIf  
```  

---

## 3. Item Creation  
**Core Cmdlet**: `New-Item`  

### Directory Creation  
```powershell  
New-Item -Path 'C:\temp\New Folder' -ItemType Directory -Force  
```  

### File Creation  
```powershell  
New-Item -Path 'C:\temp\New Folder\file.txt' -ItemType File  
```  

**Critical Behavior**:  
• `-Force` overwrites files but preserves existing directories  

---

## 4. Deletion Operations  
**Core Cmdlet**: `Remove-Item`  

### Safe Recursive Delete  
```powershell  
Remove-Item -Path C:\temp\DeleteMe -Recurse -WhatIf  
```  

### Force Cleanup  
```powershell  
Get-ChildItem -Path C:\temp\cache\* | Remove-Item -Force -Confirm:$false  
```  

---

## 5. Drive Mapping  
**Core Cmdlet**: `New-PSDrive`  

### Session-Local Mapping  
```powershell  
New-PSDrive -Name P -Root $env:ProgramFiles -PSProvider FileSystem  
Get-PSDrive -Name P  # Verify mapping  
```  

---

## 6. Data Processing  
**Core Cmdlet**: `Get-Content`  

### Text File to Array  
```powershell  
$Computers = Get-Content -Path C:\temp\DomainMembers.txt  
```  

### File Modification  
```powershell  
$ProfileContent = Get-Content -Path $PROFILE  
$ProfileContent -replace 'old_module', 'new_module' | Set-Content -Path $PROFILE  
```  

---

## Operation Standards  

| Operation Type     | Mandatory Parameters          | Safety Measures                |  
|---------------------|-------------------------------|--------------------------------|  
| **Destructive**     | `-Confirm:$false`             | `-WhatIf` + Backup Strategy    |  
| **Recursive**       | `-Recurse`                    | `-ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`|  
| **Filtering**       | `-Include`/`-Exclude`         | Pipeline to `Where-Object`     |  

---

## Validation Workflow  
```powershell  
$TestDir = "C:\temp\ps_test_$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd')"  

# Create test environment  
New-Item -Path $TestDir -ItemType Directory  
1..3 | ForEach-Object { New-Item -Path "$TestDir\file_$_.txt" -ItemType File }  

# Test copy/delete cycle  
Copy-Item -Path $TestDir -Destination "${TestDir}_backup" -Recurse -Force  
Remove-Item -Path $TestDir -Recurse -Confirm:$false  

# Verify results  
if (Test-Path -Path "${TestDir}_backup") {  
    Write-Host "Validation PASSED" -ForegroundColor Green  
}  
```  

